  "title": "Founding of Marrakesh as the Almoravid capital",
  "summary": "Marrakesh in Morocco was founded as the capital of the Almoravids, who ruled northwestern Africa and parts of southern Spain from 1056 to 1147. EBSCO and an Oxford-derived entry date the founding to 1062, crediting Yusuf ibn Tashfin, while UNESCO gives 1070-72. The Almohads took the city in 1147 and made it their capital.",
